      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "And as for why the screen may remain dark for extended periods of time, when switching instances/worlds: Queued downloads (e.g. avatars) sometimes require to finish processing as a blocking operation, before the next world/instance (\"room\") loads. This is often seen as AssetBundleDownloadManager error spam in output logs (`Error      -  [AssetBundleDownloadManager] Cannot resolve whether download 123 (1) requires a web download, assuming it doesn't.`).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-12-28T15:07:44.633Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This situation occurred when, after an operation to move an instance and the screen went dark, the screen remained dark as if the move had failed.\n\nThe first image is a screenshot taken using Windows' built-in functionality. The second image is a significantly brightened and retouched version. The third image is a screenshot taken using VRChat's built-in functionality via the F12 key.\n\nI'm Japanese so I'm not familiar with foreign memes, so at first I thought it was just the admins messing around. But a one of my  friend told me there might be some kind of hacking involved, so I'm reporting it.",
